fer to this as: region, region name, L1, geography level 1, geographic region, or region location', MODIFY COLUMN `L2` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'State associated with the service impact. L2 represents the state level in the geographic hierarchy. Users may refer to this as: state, state name, L2, geography level 2, geographic state, or state location', MODIFY COLUMN `L3` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'City associated with the service impact. L3 represents the city level in the geographic hierarchy. Users may refer to this as: city, city name, L3, geography level 3, geographic city, or city location', MODIFY COLUMN `L4` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'RF cluster associated with the service impact. L4 represents the RF cluster level in the geographic hierarchy. Users may refer to this as: RF cluster, RF cluster name, cluster, cluster name, L4, or geography level 4', MODIFY COLUMN `NODE_TYPE` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'Type of network node associated with the service impact. Users may refer to this as: node type, network element type, NE type, network node type, device type, or equipment type', MODIFY COLUMN `KPI_IMPACTED_NE` int DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'Number of network elements impacted due to KPI degradation. Users may refer to this as: KPI impacted NE, KPI impacted count, KPI affected nodes, impacted network elements, or KPI affected elements', MODIFY COLUMN `DELETED` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0' COMMENT 'Logical deletion status of the service impact detail record, where 0 indicates active and 1 indicates deleted. Users may refer to this as: deleted flag, deletion status, soft delete flag, is deleted, or active status', MODIFY COLUMN `ALARM_IMPACTED_NE` int DEFAULT NULL COMMENT 'Number of network elements impacted due to alarms. Users may refer to this as: alarm impacted NE, alarm impacted count, alarm affected nodes, impacted network elements, or alarm affected elements', MODIFY COLUMN `KPI_DATA` text COMMENT 'KPI-related data describing the service impact, typically stored in JSON format. Users may refer to this as: KPI data, KPI details, KPI impact data, KPI information, KPI payload, or KPI impact details', MODIFY COLUMN `ALARM_DATA` text COMMENT 'Alarm-related data describing the service impact, typically stored in JSON format. Users may refer to this as: alarm data, alarm details, alarm impact data, alarm information, alarm payload, or alarm impact details', MODIFY COLUMN `SERVICE_IMPACT_DASHBOARD_RULE_ID_FK` varchar(36) CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci NOT NULL COMMENT 'Identifier of the service impact dashboard rule that generated or defined this service impact record. Users may refer to this as: dashboard rule ID, service impact rule ID, rule ID, impact rule reference, or rule reference', COMMENT = 'Stores details of service impacts, including affected service information, impact status, geographic hierarchy from country and region through state and city to RF cluster, impacted network element counts, KPI and alarm impact data, and the dashboard rule associated with the impact. Users may refer to this as: service impact details, service impact information, service impact data, impacted service information, or service impact record';
